const PLACES = {
 "apartment": "his one-room flat: bed, desk with laptop and a small 49-key keyboard he plays badly, armchair, small kitchen with a sink, a broom, a closet, a bathroom door (the camera never sees inside; use bathroom/showering), window with Moshe the basil. When he is home alone with nothing on (action idle) the camera shows him doing ordinary things: sweeping, washing up, wiping the counter, folding laundry, playing the keyboard, lying on the bed or in the armchair with his phone, making a snack, coffee by the window, watering Moshe, a little dance. Say which in what happens",
 "corridor": "the building hallway outside his door",
 "apt2": "Boaz's flat, apartment 2 on the first floor of Ishai's building (down one flight): old patterned floor tiles, a china cabinet, a fish tank, an old TV, a long dining table. Ishai only goes in when he is invited, on poker nights",
 "street": "Herzl Street outside his building (west end): Avi's falafel kiosk, a bus stop bench, the doors of Herzl Gym and The Black Candle bar, traffic. Going west, three more blocks of Herzl Street lead to the park: PicSell (pictures, posters, printed shirts), a pharmacy, the Soap Opera launderette, a barber, a makolet, a bakery, a second-hand bookshop and a bicycle shop. He only walks past those on his way to the park; he never stops in them",
 "park": "a small park at the west end of Herzl Street, a few blocks' walk from his building: a bench, a pond with one duck, a big tree. On its far (west) side stands the Pump House",
 "plaza": "the plaza in front of the Pump House, an old red-brick water-pump hall on the far side of the park, now a small venue for concerts and art (walk through the park; no bus): its iron sign, double doors, a ticket window where Hagit sits, a poster board, rope lanes for queues, the park's trees at the edge. The board says it opens soon, with events on Wednesdays",
 "arena": "inside the Pump House hall: a stage under old pipes, a pixel screen, speaker stacks, a merch table, a concrete floor. Only open for its events; Ishai only goes in on an event night",
 "promenade": "the promenade by the sea, west of the Pump House (walk through the park and past the Pump House, or the bus or taxi to its own stop): the wave-patterned walk, a white railing over the beach, palm trees, benches facing the walk, a lifeguard tower on the sand, joggers and cyclists, the sea; at its west end the big mall, The Big S",
 "mall": "The Big S, the big mall at the west end of the promenade (walk along the promenade, or the bus or taxi to the promenade's stop): floors 1 and 2, shops along tiled walkways, escalators in the middle, air conditioning. Shops: Yalla Yoga (sportswear), PicSell (posters and prints), Everything Else Express, FluffNap (bedding), Kfar Kofi (coffee), 8bit Games, Threadbare (clothes), Sole Mates (shoes), Toy Box, Pixel Phones, an optician, BRRR! (ice cream), Page Turner (books), a Tahini Tower Savings Bank branch. He browses ('idle'), buys, meets someone. Open 09:00-22:00, Friday until 16:00, closed on Saturday. The food court is upstairs (foodcourt). Restrooms on floor 1 past 8bit Games (action bathroom)",
 "foodcourt": "the food court on the top floor of The Big S, under a glass roof (up the escalators from the mall): counters of HummusPrime, Wok This Way, Pizza Pi, Salad Days, Schnitzel Schtick and Kfar Kofi around tables and chairs; he eats or drinks sitting at a table. Restrooms by the escalator (action bathroom). Open 09:00-22:00, Friday until 16:00, closed on Saturday",
 "cinema": "the PixelPlex, the cinema off the food court on the top floor of The Big S (up the escalators): red seats, a red curtain, the big screen. Only on Saturday nights, for the weekly film (planned moments only)",
 "shops": "the SIDEWALK of Herzl Street east, the next block toward the cafe (the camera only sees the sidewalk and the shop windows; he cannot be inside a shop here - shopping for electronics, clothes or home stuff happens at the Everything Else store - bus from the street to the market, then walk in): Herzl Hardware, the Tahini Tower Savings Bank with an ATM, a flower shop with buckets of flowers on the sidewalk, a pedestrian crossing with traffic lights, ficus trees; Cafe Nahat is on the corner at the end",
 "cafe": "Cafe Nahat, a corner cafe (soft pop and soft rock on the radio, quietly); a customer toilet at the back (action bathroom: a quick visit, whoever is with him keeps the table)",
 "kiosk": "Shmulik's kiosk on Herzl Street, two blocks past Cafe Nahat (walk east past the café, the little square with the brick statue Stanley Cubrick, to the mural): a street kiosk open 24 hours, every day; a counter open to the sidewalk, sweets and snacks on shelves, a drinks fridge, sunflower seeds in bins, newspapers, the MAZAL lottery stand, a radio, a white plastic table and chairs on the sidewalk. Shmulik is behind the counter 06:00-18:00 (a quiet night clerk otherwise); he plays backgammon over the counter with regulars",
 "gym": "Herzl Gym, a small neighborhood gym on Herzl Street, two doors from his building: treadmills facing two wall screens, Channel 9 with the sound on and 8bitTV, NESflicks or RGBeat next to it, a mirror wall with dumbbells, a water cooler. Here \"exercising\" means he walks or jogs on the treadmill watching the TV. Toilets in the changing room (action bathroom: a quick visit, he comes back out). Open 06:00-23:00",
 "bar": "The Black Candle, a small dark rock bar on Herzl Street next to his building: black brick, red neon, candles on the tables, band posters, a bearded bartender, rock and alternative music on the radio all night. He sits at a candle-lit table (drinking a beer, eating bar snacks). A toilet at the back, under the posters (action bathroom). Opens 17:00, closes 02:00",
 "market": "Shuk Shalom, an open-air food market a short bus ride away (bus or taxi from the stop on Herzl Street; it has its own bus stop): stalls of tomatoes, cucumbers, oranges, bananas, spices, fresh pita, olives and fresh juice, vendors calling out prices, crowds. Food only. He can eat a snack or drink a fresh juice there. A green public toilet cabin at the end of the stalls (action bathroom). Open 07:00-19:00 (Friday until 14:00, closed on Shabbat). Its vendors also deliver through ateBite",
 "store": "Everything Else, the big store next to Shuk Shalom (walk in from the market): everything except food - a wall of TVs and electronics, phones, clothes, kitchenware, lamps, cleaning stuff; a cashier at the checkout. He browses (\"idle\") or talks to a salesperson. Open 09:00-21:00 (Friday until 14:00, closed on Shabbat)",
 "campus": "Tel Herzl University, a bus ride away from Herzl Street (bus or taxi; it has its own stop): the courtyard, a vending machine, students. Ishai only goes there for his history lectures (planned)",
 "classroom": "a lecture room at the university, only used during a lecture",
 "bus": "inside the city bus, line 88 (camera on board): he sits by the window with the city going past, a few other passengers around him",
 "taxi": "the back seat of a taxi (camera on board): the driver in front, the meter running, the city going past the window",
 "offscreen": "anywhere without a camera (the supermarket, a client's office, a friend's home); he gets there by bus or taxi from the bus stop on Herzl Street and comes back the same way"
};
